[agent] ## Summary
[agent] All real comparison work ran on the platform: I ingested both CSVs into Hopsworks feature groups (`train_features`, `serve_features`) via `hops fg insert`, then compared them with a Trino join over the offline store (`hops sql`).
[agent] **Finding:** Across all 200 entities present in both feature groups, features `f1`, `f2`, `f3`, `f5` are identical (mean absolute difference = 0.0). Only **f4** diverges (mean abs diff ≈ 7.78).
[agent] **Cause:** The skew is a missing transformation in the serving path. The relationship is exact: `serve_f4 = exp(train_f4) − 1 = expm1(train_f4)` (verified platform-side, max abs error 2.4e-5 = CSV rounding). So the training pipeline computes `f4 = log1p(raw)` (log of the raw value), while the online serving path emits the **raw, untransformed** value — classic train/serve skew from a transform applied in training but not in serving.
